<article class="league-type">
  <p class="league-type__kicker">DESIGN LAB / LEAGUE MONO / RELEASE 2.300</p>
  <h1>League Mono</h1>
  <p class="league-type__intro">A variable monospace face by <a href="https://github.com/theleagueof/league-mono">Tyler Finck and The League of Moveable Type</a>. Try its width and weight against actual headings, supporting labels and code. The site keeps Anton for display and Plex Sans for reading; League Mono supplies code and metadata.</p>
  <div class="league-type__controls" data-pagefind-ignore>
    <label for="league-width">Width: <output id="league-width-value" for="league-width">100%</output></label>
    <input type="range" id="league-width" min="50" max="200" value="100" step="1" aria-describedby="league-width-help">
    <div class="league-type__range-ends"><span>50 / condensed</span><span>200 / extended</span></div>
    <p id="league-width-help">Controls the font’s real <code>wdth</code> axis through CSS <code>font-stretch</code>.</p>
    <label for="league-weight">Weight: <output id="league-weight-value" for="league-weight">400</output></label>
    <input type="range" id="league-weight" min="100" max="800" value="400" step="1" aria-describedby="league-weight-help">
    <div class="league-type__range-ends"><span>100 / thin</span><span>800 / extra bold</span></div>
    <p id="league-weight-help">Controls the font’s real <code>wght</code> axis through CSS <code>font-weight</code>.</p>
    <label for="league-text">Try your own text</label>
    <input type="text" id="league-text" value="Make it make sense." maxlength="140">
    <p id="league-font-status" role="status">Loading the local variable font…</p>
  </div>
  <p class="league-type__sample league-type__hero" id="league-live">Make it make sense.</p>
  <section class="league-type__row" aria-labelledby="league-real-text">
    <h2 id="league-real-text">Headlines and supporting text</h2>
    <p class="league-type__sample">Platforms. Content. People.</p>
    <p class="league-type__sample">Ideas in circulation</p>
    <p class="league-type__sample">One shared truth for Storybook and Figma</p>
    <p class="league-type__sample">16 Nov 2026 · 1,234 words · Bonn, Germany</p>
  </section>
  <section class="league-type__row" aria-labelledby="league-code-heading">
    <h2 id="league-code-heading">Code and ambiguous characters</h2>
    <pre class="league-type__sample league-type__code"><code>const page = { title: "Make it make sense.", width: 100 };
for (let i = 0; i &lt; 10; i++) {
  console.log(`${i}: ${page.title}`);
}
// 0O 1Il | {} [] () &lt;&gt; != === =&gt; /* comment */
--kh-font-mono: 'League Mono', monospace;</code></pre>
    <p class="league-type__sample">ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ<br>abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz<br>0123456789 0O 1Il<br>ä ö ü ß é è ç ñ ø Å Æ Œ</p>
  </section>
  <section class="league-type__row league-type__notes" aria-labelledby="league-font-notes">
    <h2 id="league-font-notes">The actual file, not assumed ranges</h2>
    <p>The unmodified upstream WOFF2 contains 546 encoded code points. Inspection of its <code>fvar</code> table gives weight 100–800, default 100, and width 50–200, default 50. This specimen deliberately starts at weight 400 and width 100. There is no slant or optical-size axis in this file.</p>
    <p>The complete release font is self-hosted, without subsetting or new outlines. Characters outside its coverage use the fallback face. Code lines keep their formatting and scroll within the sample at wide settings; prose samples wrap.</p>
    <p><a href="/assets/kh-font/league-mono/LeagueMono-VF.woff2">Download variable WOFF2</a> · <a href="/assets/kh-font/league-mono/LeagueMono-VF.ttf">Download variable TTF</a> · <a href="/assets/kh-font/league-mono/OFL.md">Original SIL Open Font License</a> · <a href="https://github.com/theleagueof/league-mono/releases/tag/2.300">Upstream release</a></p>
  </section>
</article>
<script>
(() => {
  const lab = document.querySelector('.league-type');
  const width = document.getElementById('league-width');
  const weight = document.getElementById('league-weight');
  const text = document.getElementById('league-text');
  const live = document.getElementById('league-live');
  width.addEventListener('input', () => {
    lab.style.setProperty('--league-width', width.value);
    document.getElementById('league-width-value').value = `${width.value}%`;
  });
  weight.addEventListener('input', () => {
    lab.style.setProperty('--league-weight', weight.value);
    document.getElementById('league-weight-value').value = weight.value;
  });
  text.addEventListener('input', () => { live.textContent = text.value || 'Make it make sense.'; });
  document.fonts.load('400 48px "League Mono"', 'Make it make sense.').then(fonts => {
    document.getElementById('league-font-status').textContent = fonts.length ? 'Local League Mono loaded. Width 50–200; weight 100–800.' : 'The font did not load; you are seeing the fallback.';
  }).catch(() => {
    document.getElementById('league-font-status').textContent = 'The font did not load; you are seeing the fallback.';
  });
})();
</script>
